    "whatIsAg": {
        "visited": false,
        "dialogue": [
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Agency generally refers to being a goal-directed, intentional entity capable of acting."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Critically, moral agency is the capacity to make normative judgments about right and wrong and respond to them."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Some suggest this is required for an entity to be &ldquo;fit to be held responsible&rdquo;, and conceptually, there's no reason an AI couldn't achieve it."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Some also include &ldquo;agency&rdquo; (having preferences, desires, and plans one acts upon) as potentially sufficient for moral standing, distinct from sentience."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Would you like to discuss another cognitive capability?"
            }
        ],
